<title>TURKEY: Turk Demirbank 1996 profits rise 120 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Demirbank 1996 profits rise 120 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     1,823.35   vs  2,281.47</p>
<p>    Net profit		     10,028.44   vs  4,562.95</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  34,198.94   vs 14,415.70</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense   23,166.65   vs  9,852.75</p>
<p>    Deposits			 84,397.07   vs 29,120.83</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		 34,306.81   vs 10,351.27</p>
<p>    Equity			    8,199.68   vs  2,604.88</p>
<p>    Capital			   5,500.00   vs  2,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE: Shares of Demirbank, which is owned 74.31 percent by Turkish Cingilli Holding, are also listed on the  Munich bourse. The bank initiated a Level 1 ADR programme on U.S. bourses late last year and seeks listing of the ADRs on the Frankfurt bourse.</p>
<p>The figures do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
